      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nEmit `BlockRemoved` only when the last physical copy of a prefix-cache hash disappears. This keeps KV-event consumers from discarding a prefix that the engine still caches.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Evicting one of several copies leaves the external hash resident until the final copy disappears.\n- The guard applies to eviction and partial-prefix replacement or promotion through the shared event emitter.\n- The change preserves the event schema, cache-group isolation, `BlockStored` behavior, and the internal `pop` contract.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe existing eviction test checks that the first duplicate removal emits no event and the final removal emits the expected hash. It also checks single-copy removals.\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py \\\n  -k 'maybe_evict_cached_block or kv_cache_events' -q --confcutdir=tests/v1/core\n.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/distributed/test_kv_cache_events.py \\\n  -q --confcutdir=tests/distributed\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\n  tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py vllm/v1/core/block_pool.py\n```\n\nThe refreshed branch passes the selected eviction/event tests (7 passed, 158 deselected) and event-schema tests (17 passed). The repository pre-commit hooks pass on both changed files.\n\nEnd-to-end serving validation is pending for this revision. The unit commands exclude the root `tests/conftest.py` because the available environment lacks `tblib`. The regression already runs in the Buildkite CPU job.\n\n## Details\n\nvLLM can keep several physical blocks for the same prefix hash. On current `main`, removing any copy emits `BlockRemoved`, even while another copy remains available. A router that treats this event as hash eviction can underestimate the engine's cached prefix and choose another engine. This PR makes no throughput or latency claim.\n\nThe shared emitter checks the existing hash map after removal. The key includes the cache group, so another group's copy cannot suppress an event. Event-disabled execution returns before the added lookup. Event-enabled removal adds one dictionary lookup per removed hash. Hash relocation remains event-free. Both model runners use this scheduler-side cache pool, so a separate MRV2 change is unnecessary.\n\nThis existing PR overlaps [#55092](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/55092), which fixes the same behavior through copy counts. This version retains the existing map-removal contract and adds a guard in the event emitter. The overlap needs maintainer coordination before either equivalent fix merges.\n\nAI assistance was used for the code and this refresh. The submitter still needs to review the refreshed diff and complete end-to-end validation.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\n",
